From c68b32f91805174c9d5cb823b379e3ca7f78b2ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:48:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/53] B70-IP-H1: lm_head as INT8 W8A8 (B70_HEAD_INT8=1),
 native int8 DPAS

The FP8 W8A16 head upcasts e4m3 to bf16 (storage only). Per-row int8
weights (one scale per vocab row) + per-token int8 activations through the
B70-IP-W1 opaque op (Triton int8 at decode M, oneDNN int8_scaled_mm above):
same bytes as FP8, int8 math on XMX, and per-row int8 is ~4x more accurate
than e4m3 on embedding-like rows (PLE study 0.66% vs 2.66% rel-L2). Built
once at the first forward, BF16 shard released first; wins over
B70_HEAD_FP8 when both are set. Drafters sharing the head use it too.
QFN path only (qwen4_exp); CPU test included, GPU pending.
